voynich-eva: license

Dataset: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

  VCAT's annotations in this repository's configurations (the metadata's
  section judgements and missing folios, the links to Yale's images, the
  mismatch verdicts and scores, the variant tables' agreement, baseline and
  alignments) are CC-BY-4.0. The lines (default), the words and the
  per-source transliterations are the text of the transliterations of the
  Voynich Manuscript (Beinecke MS 408, Yale University) as voynich.nu
  publishes them, and functions of it; voynich.nu makes them available under
  CC0 (CC0-1.0), and those fields stay CC0 wherever they are reused. The
  statement and where it was read are recorded in data_sources/sources.yaml
  and docs/SOURCES_LICENSE.md of the repository; it was read at its source on
  2026-10-17.

  Please cite the transliterators named in the dataset card in published work.

Code that builds the data: MIT License
  https://github.com/noah-chelednik/voynich-data/blob/main/LICENSE

The manuscript itself is in the public domain.
